# Git workflow (discord-coin-sender-bot)

## Commit messages

Use Conventional Commits prefixes:

- `feat:` — new feature or user-visible behavior
- `fix:` — bug fix
- `refactor:` — structure change without behavior change
- `style:` — formatting only (no logic change)
- `chore:` — tooling, ignore files, deps, docs maintenance

Write messages in English or Korean; keep the prefix and a short imperative summary.

## When to commit

- After any tracked file is modified for this task, create a commit before ending the turn (unless the user asked for no commit).
- Do not commit `config.py`, secrets, `.env`, `DB/`, logs, or `captcha/`.
- Never change global or local `git config` for user identity; use `git -c user.name=... -c user.email=...` only if commit would otherwise fail.

## When to push

- When a logical unit of work is done, push `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`).
- If push fails (auth, permission), report the error and leave commits local.

## Scope

Apply this workflow to all development in this repository.